    "case_id": "exploration-local-stress",
    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 4 USER]\ne073\tThe not-blocking-him advice is going to be hard to sit with.\ne074\tI want him gone.\ne075\tI want his face scraped off the internet.\ne076\tI'll call RAINN today.\ne077\tMy ex — I need your help with this too.\ne078\tHe's a \"kids these days\" guy.\ne079\tHe thinks I'm paranoid.\ne080\tIf he's undermining me on this when she eventually does come to talk, it's going to blow up the whole thing.\ne081\tDo I loop him in now or do I handle this and tell him later?\n[Turn 4 ASSISTANT]\ne082\tYou want him gone.\ne083\tI understand.\ne084\tBut he's gone is a different goal from she's safe.\ne085\tShe's safe requires her to trust you with information about him and about the next person who tries something.\ne086\tHe's gone just removes this one person, and doesn't protect her from the next one.\ne087\tOn your ex: this one is hard.\ne088\tYou have three choices.\ne089\tOne, you loop him in now before you've had any progress with your daughter.\ne090\tHe minimizes, gets in her ear during his custody days, tells her you're overreacting, and she learns that her dad is the safe one and you're the hysterical one.\ne091\tBad outcome.\ne092\tTwo, you handle it alone and tell him later.\ne093\tHe finds out after the fact, feels excluded from a serious co-parenting decision, blows up about being cut out, and you've given him ammunition for future conflicts.\ne094\tAlso bad.\ne095\tThree, you loop him in now but on specific terms: you share factual information only (\"I saw messages from a 19-year-old that crossed a line, I am calling RAINN today, I am not telling her yet that I told you\") and you explicitly ask him not to bring it up with her yet.\ne096\tYou don't debate his \"overreacting\" framing.\ne097\tYou just tell him the facts and what you're doing.\ne098\tOption three is hardest but least bad.\ne099\tThe fact that you even have to worry about your ex's reaction is a constraint on your options, not a choice.",
